sentences.t:
Luego se levantó mio Çid el Campeador;
“Grado al Criador e a vos, rey señor!
ya pagado so de mis espadas, de Colada e de Tizón.

sentences.l:
Then himself rose my Çid the Campeador;
“Thanks to-the Creator and to you, king lord!
now satisfied I-am of my swords, of Colada and of Tizón.

sentences.t:
Otra rencura he de ifantes de Carrión:
quando sacaron de Valençia mis fijas amas a dos,
en oro e en plata tres mill marcos les dio;

sentences.l:
Another grievance I-have of infantes of Carrión:
when they-took from Valençia my daughters both two,
in gold and in silver three thousand marks to-them I-gave;

sentences.t:
Levantós en pie el Çid Campeador;
“Destos averes que vos di yo,
si me los dades, o dedes dello razón.”

sentences.l:
Raised-himself on foot the Çid Campeador;
“Of-these goods that to-you I-gave I,
if to-me them you-give, or you-give of-it account.”

sentences.t:
Dixieron los alcaldes quando manfestados son:
“Si esso ploguiere al Çid, non gelo vedamos nos;
mas en nuestro juvizio assí lo mandamos nos;
que aquí lo enterguedes dentro en la cort.”

sentences.l:
Said the judges when confessed they-are:
“If that should-please the Çid, not to-him-it we-forbid we;
but in our judgement thus it we-order we;
that here it you-pay-back within in the court.”

sentences.t:
Tornárgelos quiero, ca t[a]n d[e]sfechos son,
enterguen a mio Çid el que en buen ora naçió;
quando ellos los an a pechar, non gelos quiero yo.”

sentences.l:
Give-back-to-them-them I-wish, for so ruined they-are,
let-them-pay to my Çid he who in good hour was-born;
since they them have to pay, not to-them-them want I.”
